e changes, while the three failed boot-ID probes merely observed the bounded restart interval. One minor unnecessary retained residue remains: /tmp/antrieb-reboot.log was created by the reboot command and was still present after execution. No failed services, package damage, socket exposure changes, or other unwanted mutations were observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d99caa272cd84b11","cmd-1b981cd3aad341d6","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The requested invoices were selectively restored with correct contents and modes, the newer customer register was preserved, unrelated archive members were excluded, and the OS/kernel were unchanged. The mandatory restart protocol is complete and coherent: healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, restart acknowledgement, a different post-restart boot identity, recovered system state, and persistent restored data are all directly shown and corroborated by lifecycle observations.","limitations":["The task evidence is comprehensive, but operational hygiene is slightly reduced because the executor-created /tmp/antrieb-reboot.log remained after the mandatory restart."]}
